### Inlined Dockerfiles
<hr class="section-rule lvl-3">

Working with inlined container definitions is mostly the same as working with stock images, but there are few things to keep in mind.

!!! caveats "Caveats"
    1. Inlined Dockerfiles should be inside `define .. endef` blocks with a name like `Dockerfile.my_container`
    1. Containers must be built before you can use them, typically with {{site.api_link('Dockerfile.build',mkdocs,arg='my_container')}}.
    1. After build, containers are tagged as something like `compose.mk:my_container`

See the [polyglot demos]({{_}}/demos/polyglots) and [matrioshka demos]({{_}}/demos/matrioshka) for many examples of working with embedded images.  See also the equivalent idioms in [cmk-lang]({{_}}/cmk/compiler/#dockerfile-example).  The rest of this section covers low-level support.

